# Line-ending policy, added when Windows joined the supported platforms.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which converts LF to CRLF on
# checkout and back on commit. That round-trip is usually invisible — until a
# file's *bytes* are load-bearing. Two places here they are:
#
#   * spec JSON is hashed into run provenance, so a CRLF copy of an unchanged
#     spec produces a different digest and a Windows user's sweep stops matching
#     a colleague's for a reason that has nothing to do with the science;
#   * tests/reference_values.json holds the exact numerical baselines that KS
#     rule 3 forbids re-recording without sign-off.
#
# Normalising to LF in the repository keeps the stored bytes identical on every
# platform. Working trees are unaffected on macOS and Linux, and MSVC, GCC and
# Clang all compile LF sources without complaint.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats: never transform these, whatever the platform.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.bin binary
*.metallib binary
*.npy binary
*.npz binary

# Notebooks are JSON, but they are diffed and merged often enough that it is
# worth being explicit rather than relying on content sniffing.
*.ipynb text eol=lf
